{"additions":58,"changedFiles":3,"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T05:39:23Z","authors":[{"email":"225494842+fresfrida@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDODXDHOg","login":"fresfrida","name":"Frescylia Frida"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T05:39:23Z","messageBody":"- Externalise every English string on ProofScreen under en.json proof.check.*\n  (button, checking, described.title/note, verified.match/diff/savedLabel/\n  newLabel, error, disclosure) using {{name}} for the dog's name. Rephrases\n  the comparison so it matches PRD 7.4: the photo is saved as proof, the\n  app never identifies a pill, and the user is always told to check the\n  package and ask their pharmacist.\n- Drop the similarity percentage from the verified result card.\n- On error, surface proof.check.error and console.warn the raw detail\n  instead of rendering it to the senior. State no longer carries the\n  message field.\n- Move the inline styles in the pill check block to the existing\n  stylesheet (.proof-photo-preview, .proof-photo-input,\n  .proof-check-block, .proof-check-card, .proof-check-card-title,\n  .proof-check-card-line, .proof-check-card-note,\n  .proof-checking-status, .proof-check-error,\n  .proof-check-disclosure). No hex colours in the component; reuses\n  existing colour tokens (sage, text, action-stop).\n- `Give {{name}} a heart` continues to render and call onVerified\n  independently of the check state.\n- Skipped mock/milestones.ts `Just Buddy` rename per the follow-up;\n  another branch owns it.","messageHeadline":"ProofScreen: pill check wording per PRD 7.4 (proof.check.*)","oid":"0bbdd4e04619fff018301c5a49866488d8d00b61"}],"deletions":30,"headRefName":"cb/pill-check-wording","state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/whansel007/Pawtner/pull/28"}
